Refinements to your amendments:

Point	Refinement
2. Snapshot history	Profile it first (P1 below), because the result removes or keeps whole test families. Reconstructed history only ever yields “first observed at reporting date X”, which is an upper bound on when something changed. It never yields an event date.
6. Cancellation timing	Agreed. ACT_MODIFICATION_DT is recorded as “last modified” and is never used as a cancellation date. Whether ACT_CLOSURE_DT is populated for cancelled actions is a profiling question, and its meaning needs a data-owner answer.
8. Task-specific usability	Raters score the same 50 cases per domain, and each field is rated only against the tasks it feeds. This keeps rater load near the original.
10. Leakage	Two fields are both useful signals and leakage candidates: ACTNS_TO_PRVNT_REOCURNC (incident) and ISS_INC_ASSOC_LIST. Profile when they changed relative to issue closure, using first-appearance across snapshots if history allows.
14. Small counts	Secure output carries exact counts. Shared output carries banded counts, with the threshold set by the privacy policy owner. I use 10 as a placeholder only.

